  "summary": "No listed instrument can perform non-destructive 3D internal imaging of bulk, opaque specimens; X-ray micro-computed tomography (micro-CT) is the standard technique for this. If your specimen is transparent or fluorescently labeled, confocal or multiphoton microscopy can provide non-destructive 3D views of the internal structure, though only to a depth of a few hundred micrometres."
}

